## Decisions and Action Items

1.  **Liaison Statement**: The working group will send a liaison statement to MPEG indicating plans to optimize CMAF compression overhead via LocMAF (`draft-ietf-moq-loc`). A call for working group adoption of `draft-ietf-moq-loc` will be initiated after receiving MPEG's response.
2.  **Draft 21 & 22 Publishing**: The editors will publish Draft 21 of `draft-ietf-moq-transport` as a "pure move" document (reflecting only reordering). Draft 22, containing the editorial cleanups and clarifications, will be published immediately after to maintain clear git history.
3.  **Seattle Interop Target**: The target for the Seattle interop is set to Draft 20. No further wire-breaking pull requests will be merged into the main branch until after the interop.
4.  **Split PR #1625**: Editors will split the forward parameter PR into an editorial/terminology PR (ready to land) and a technical PR on location filter pausing (needs work).
5.  **Refine PR #1620**: Editors will update the publisher priority PR to restrict priority changes to group boundaries and remove the associated "malformed track" errors.
6.  **URI Scheme Relocation**: Cullen Jennings will work on incorporating the MoQ URI scheme definition from `draft-ietf-moq-transport` into `draft-jennings-moq-resolution-00`.